**Decisions the task didn't specify**

- Expiry is inclusive at the boundary: an entry is absent when `now() >= expiresAt` (expires at exactly `ttlMs` after set, per "expiring ttlMs after it was set").
- An expired entry that was never touched still occupies an LRU slot until it's overwritten or evicted — `set` evicts the least-recently-used slot regardless of whether that entry has expired. Since expired entries read as absent either way, this can't leak values; it only means the slot chosen for eviction may be an already-expired one, which is the most useful choice.
- `size` counts live entries without mutating the map, so expired entries don't get purged lazily by a read-only call.
